    "final_answer": "I have found the latest news on arXiv. Here are the findings:\n\n## Latest News from arXiv\n\nBased on the **arXiv Blog** (blog.arxiv.org), the most recent news is dated **September 23, 2026**:\n\n### 🆕 Headline: \"arXiv receives Multiyear Philanthropic Commitments to Support Its Launch as an Independent Nonprofit\"\n**Author:** Kat Boboris\n\n**Key points of the announcement:**\n- arXiv announced that **three leading philanthropic organizations** have provided multimillion-dollar support:\n  - **Simons Foundation International**\n  - **XTX Markets**\n  - **Siegel Family Endowment**\n- Total commitment: **$17.2 million** spanning 3 to 5 years\n- The funds will support:\n  - Platform development\n  - Organizational capacity\n  - Technical infrastructure\n  - Ongoing operations\n  - Services for researchers worldwide\n- This is connected to arXiv's transition into an independent nonprofit after 3.5 decades of operation\n- Penelope Lewis is named as the **Chief Executive Officer of arXiv**\n\n---\n\n### Other Recent arXiv Blog Posts:\n1. **Sept 3, 2026** — \"Attention Authors: Temporary changes to announcements\" (effective Sept 7, 2026)\n2. **Sept 1, 2026** — \"We're Hiring! Associate Production Editor\"\n3. **July 30, 2026** — \"arXiv welcomes inaugural CEO and Board of Directors\"\n4. Earlier posts include: \"Remembering Ralph Wijers\", \"arXiv now hosts over 3 million articles\", and \"arXiv's next chapter: Updates on our spin out from Cornell\"\n\nAdditionally, on the arXiv homepage, a banner announcement is displayed: **\"arXiv is now an independent nonprofit!\"** with a \"Learn more\" link pointing to the About page — confirming the same major news about arXiv becoming an independent nonprofit.",
